# Anchor `lib/` + `lib64/` to the project root. The unanchored form
# `lib/` is basename-matched at EVERY directory level, so it silently
# swallows `sau_web/frontend/src/lib/` (utils.ts, tone.ts,
# chatFormBridge.ts, etc.) which is hand-written source code that the
# Vite build imports via `@/lib/...` aliases. Without the leading
# `/`, `git add -A` skips the whole `src/lib/` tree and remote builds
# fail with "Cannot find module @/lib/chat/chatFormBridge" until
# someone force-adds the file with `git add -f`.
#
# Anchoring to project root preserves the original intent (ignore the
# top-level `lib/` + `lib64/` that `pip install --user` or virtualenvs
# create) while letting the frontend's `src/lib/` participate in git
# as ordinary source.
#
# Tracked in the chore(tsc-debt) round — the chatFormBridge.ts
# re-export fix that resolves 1 of the 12 pre-existing tsc errors
# requires this rule to be in place.
/lib/
/lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
