# ── Pre-push hardening (round-OPT-seedance-export) ──
# 1. Live-credentials backup: `.env.bak` mirrors the real `.env`
#    — block the FILE pattern. The directory-only `env.bak/`
#    entry at line 128 catches dirs but NOT files, which let a
#    plaintext credential copy leak through past `git add -A`.
#    `*.bak` blanket-covers any future backup convention.
.env.bak
*.bak

# 2. Studio render artifacts: `media/studio/<pid>/render.mp4`
#    + per-scene mp3/png grow into hundreds of MB; never stage.
media/

# 3. Personal session meta (saved plans + thoughts from the
#    agent loop) — keeps the public repo focused on shipped
#    code only.
.mimocode/

# 4. Noise files like `=1.3`, `=1.8`, `=2.0` left over from
#    past scratch sessions — harmless but they pollute
#    `git status`. (NOTE: bare `=` would only match a file
#    LITERALLY named `=` — gitignore without `/` is basename-
#    anchored. The `=*` glob is the correct shape to swallow
#    every `=<digits>.<digits>` leftover and any other
#    `=`-prefixed scratch file.)
=*
